<!-- Event 2 (supply shortage), RETIMED to 13:00-14:30 (46800-52200 s).

     Identical to 2023-07-04_event_accident.add.xml in every respect but the
     interval: same edge 29119849#1, same lanes _3 and _4, same
     allow="authority", same 90-minute duration.

     Why it was retimed (docs/9, 2026-08-21). The original ran 08:00-09:30, but
     a GNN sample needs 24 history bins of 300 s and the simulation begins at
     07:00, so the earliest sample whose target can be scored is anchored at
     09:00. Counting target bins by the builder's convention
     (src/prediction/unclipped_truth.py), the 08:00 closure reaches only 15 of
     684 target bins (2.2%) and per horizon step h1..h6 = 5, 4, 3, 2, 1, 0. No
     sample has both ends of the h1->h6 change disturbed, so the change metric
     the event evaluation reports was never measured across a disturbed
     interval, and the first 60 of the closure's 90 minutes existed only inside
     the first sample's input history. The onset, the part with forecasting
     value, was never a prediction target.

     Why 13:00 and not an earlier simulation start. Starting the run at 06:00
     would keep the morning peak, but every training day starts at 07:00 and so
     carries samples from 09:00 only. A test day scored from 08:00 would be
     predicting a time of day the model has never trained on, which would
     confound the disruption with an unseen input distribution.

     13:00-14:30 gives 23 of 114 samples touching the closure, 108 of 684 target
     bins (15.8%), and 13 samples with all six bins inside it. The start also
     matches the corridor and cordon slowdowns (46800-50400), so the three
     disruptions become comparable in time of day.

     The trade is real and should be stated wherever this is used: midday
     carries less demand than the morning peak, so the same closure bites less
     hard. What it buys is that the closure is measured at all.

     Pinned by tests/routing/test_event_injection.py. -->
<additional>
  <rerouter id="accident_0704_midday" edges="29119849#1">
    <interval begin="46800" end="52200">
      <closingLaneReroute id="29119849#1_3" allow="authority"/>
      <closingLaneReroute id="29119849#1_4" allow="authority"/>
    </interval>
  </rerouter>
</additional>
